1
00:00:00,007 --> 00:00:07,892
NurseGlance: a nurse-centered ICU handoff dashboard built on HL7 FHIR data. Research prototype, not for clinical use.

2
00:00:07,899 --> 00:00:16,616
The control: a tabbed EHR-style view of the same FHIR data, here for a ventilated patient on two vasopressors.

3
00:00:16,622 --> 00:00:22,422
Vitals sit in flowsheet groups, one table per group, newest column first.

4
00:00:22,427 --> 00:00:29,479
Labs are one long table: 94 results for this patient in the last 72 hours.

5
00:00:29,484 --> 00:00:38,202
Drips and doses are under another tab, in sections. Answering one handoff question can mean several tabs and scrolls.

6
00:00:38,207 --> 00:00:44,299
NurseGlance shows the same patient on one screen, organized by organ system.

7
00:00:44,302 --> 00:00:54,688
At the top: every infusion running now with its rate, and the next dose of each drug in the 12 hours after handoff.

8
00:00:54,693 --> 00:01:06,328
Each value shows the latest reading, a trend arrow, the 12-hour range and a sparkline. An H or L badge marks a value outside its threshold.

9
00:01:06,333 --> 00:01:12,343
Drips show their rate, the last titration and when they started.

10
00:01:12,347 --> 00:01:21,483
"None", "not charted" and "not in FHIR demo" stay separate, so a true negative is never mistaken for missing data.

11
00:01:22,554 --> 00:01:32,522
Below the panels, a 12-hour timeline shows each dose and infusion after handoff. Pointing at a dose shows its name and time.

12
00:01:32,527 --> 00:01:43,744
Optional rule-based flags. Each one shows its rule, the values, their times and FHIR ids. Thresholds are placeholders, and flags are off in study mode.

13
00:01:43,749 --> 00:01:49,039
Study mode runs an AWARE-style crossover session, start to finish.

14
00:01:49,043 --> 00:01:55,678
A logged seed sets the view order and which patients go with each view.

15
00:01:55,683 --> 00:02:03,152
The question stays beside the view. Every click, screen and answer is logged with its time.

16
00:02:03,158 --> 00:02:10,204
Here the answer is in the infusion strip: norepinephrine 0.2 mcg/kg/min.

17
00:02:10,208 --> 00:02:18,509
After each view come the System Usability Scale and NASA-TLX, and the session exports CSV files for analysis.

18
00:02:18,513 --> 00:02:28,891
Virtual-nurse mode: admission and discharge checklists, a session timer, and a break prompt at 10 minutes.

19
00:02:28,896 --> 00:02:37,614
Virtual nurses showed cognitive fatigue within about 10 to 12 minutes of an encounter in a 2025 eye-tracking study.

20
00:02:37,625 --> 00:02:56,760
So far: FHIR can supply 57 of 58 handoff elements. Scripted expert paths take 3.2 s per question in NurseGlance against 12.9 s in the tabbed view (design-level estimates, not nurse data). Next: a crossover study with ICU and virtual nurses, after IRB approval.

21
00:02:56,772 --> 00:03:02,773
Code, reports and protocol: github.com/ibrahimbaabdullah-jpg/nurseglance.
